// Package flatbuffers implements a thin passthrough codec for already-encoded
// FlatBuffer payloads. The universal Codec contract speaks `any`, but
// FlatBuffers is a schema-driven format whose typed access lives in caller
// code (generated by `flatc`). This package therefore registers a codec that
// round-trips raw FlatBuffer bytes — Marshal hands back the buffer the caller
// already has; Unmarshal publishes the buffer to the caller's target without
// parsing it. Real schema-typed reads stay in the caller's generated
// accessors.
//
// The codec uses no third-party dependency. The only validation is the
// 4-byte root-offset header required by the FlatBuffers wire format.
//
// Package flatbuffers — small adapter interfaces that let strongly-typed
// FlatBuffers wrappers participate in the universal codec contract without
// reaching into schema-generated structs from this package.
package flatbuffers
